{"kind":"assert","text":"NOW priority-1 ruling on Artifacts bounds. The shape is approved: ArtifactsProvider.objects counts unique body bytes and objects cumulatively and stops before it materializes the next body that would cross either bound. Verified object identity stays unchanged. Use the namespace's configured maxBytes (10,485,760 in each Worker's ARTIFACTS_CONFIG) as the byte bound and the existing Reader.closure count bound as the object bound. Add no new setting. An over-budget adoption stops with one typed refusal that is distinct from transport failure. It records nothing and sends nothing, and the witness proves both. If the workspace closure already has a stop class for its own budget, reuse that name. Before source, report the largest current closure on the live namespaces in bytes and objects. If any live closure exceeds half of either bound, stop and report instead of building. Journal reads and GitHub synchronization keep their own owners.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}